            %p
          %p
          .proof
            %h6 Proof
            %p
              By
              %a.maruku-eqref{:href => "#eq:EigenvaluesAtLogIntegerInverseTempeteratureCountingYoungTableaux"} (12)
              in Prop.
              %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#EigenvaluesAtLogIntegerInvTemViaYoungTabl"}
              the eigenvalues at
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi β
                    %mo =
                    %mi ln
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi N
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \beta = ln(N)
              count possible numbers of colorings of Young diagrams to
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/semistandard+Young+tableaux"} semistandard Young tableaux
              (ssYT). This gives the first statement.
            %p Since in a ssYT the labels must strictly increase downwards, there is no possible ssYT-coloring if there are fewer labels than rows. This gives the second claim.
            %p But conversely, since in an ssYT the labels may be constant horizontally, there is at least one coloring once there never are more rows than labels. This gives the last claim.
          %p
            %br/
          %p
            We give further
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/combinatorics"} combinatorial
            expressions of the eigenvalues of the Cayley distance kernel, using the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/hook+length+formula"} hook length formula
            and the
            = succeed ":" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/hook-content+formula"} hook-content formula
          %p
          #EigenvaluesInTermsOfHookContent.num_prop
            %h6 Proposition
            %p
              %strong
                (Eigenvalues of Cayley distance kernel via
                = succeed ")" do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/hook-content+formula"} hook-content formula
            %p
              The eigenvalues
              %a.maruku-eqref{:href => "#eq:CharacterFormulaForEigenvalueOfCayleyDistanceKernel"} (10)
              of the Cayley distance kernel for all
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msup
                      %mi e
                      %mi β
                    %mo ∈
                    %msub
                      %mi ℝ
                      %mo +
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} e^\beta \in \mathbb{R}_+
              may be expressed as:
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi EigVals
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                    %msup
                      %mi e
                      %mrow
                        %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                        %mi β
                        %mo ⋅
                        %msub
                          %mi d
                          %mi C
                    %msub
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                      %mi λ
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %mo =
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %mfrac
                      %mrow
                        %mi n
                        %mo !
                      %mrow
                        %msup
                          %mi χ
                          %mrow
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                            %mi λ
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %msup
                      %mi e
                      %mrow
                        %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                        %mi β
                        %mo ⋅
                        %mi N
                    %munder
                      %mo{:lspace => "thinmathspace", :rspace => "thinmathspace"} ∏
                      %mfrac{:linethickness => "0"}
                        %mrow
                          %mrow
                            %mn 1
                            %mo ≤
                            %mi i
                            %mo ≤
                            %mi rows
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                            %mi λ
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                        %mrow
                          %mrow
                            %mn 1
                            %mo ≤
                            %mi j
                            %mo ≤
                            %msub
                              %mi λ
                              %mi i
                    %mfrac
                      %mrow
                        %msup
                          %mi e
                          %mi β
                        %mo +
                        %mi j
                        %mo −
                        %mi i
                      %mrow
                        %mi ℓ
                        %msub
                          %mi hook
                          %mi λ
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %mi i
                        %mo ,
                        %mi j
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                    %mo .
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    EigVals[e^{- \beta \cdot d_C}]_\lambda
                    \\;=\;
                    \\frac
                    {n!}
                    {\chi^{(\lambda)}}
                    e^{- \beta \cdot N}
                    \\underset
                    {
                    { 1 \leq i \leq rows(\lambda) }
                    \\atop
                    { 1 \leq j \leq \lambda_i }
                    }
                    {\prod}
                    \\frac{
                    e^{\beta}+ j - i
                    }{
                    \\ell hook_\lambda(i,j)
                    }
                    \\,.
            %p
          The following proof was pointed out by
          = succeed "." do
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Abdelmalek+Abdesselam"} Abdelmalek Abdesselam
          .proof
            %h6 Proof
            %p
              By Prop.
              %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#EigenvaluesAtLogIntegerInvTemViaYoungTabl"}
              the
              = succeed "th" do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi λ
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \lambda
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msup
                      %mi e
                      %mi β
                    %mo =
                    %mi N
                    %mo ∈
                    %msub
                      %mi ℕ
                      %mo +
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    e^{\beta} = N \in \mathbb{N}_+
            %p
              is a positive multiple of the number of semi-standard Young tableau, and hence is given by the
              = succeed "," do
                %em
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/hook-content+formula"} hook-content formula
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mrow
                      %mtable{:columnalign => "right left right left right left right left right left", :columnspacing => "0em", :displaystyle => "true"}
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                            %mfrac
                              %mrow
                                %msup
                                  %mi χ
                                  %mrow
                                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                                    %mi λ
                                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                                %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                                %mi e
                                %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                              %mrow
                                %mi n
                                %mo !
                            %msup
                              %mi N
                              %mi n
                            %mo ⋅
                            %mi EigVals
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                            %msup
                              %mi e
                              %mrow
                                %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                                %mi ln
                                %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                                %mi N
                                %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                            %mo ⋅
                            %msub
                              %mi d
                              %mi C
                            %msub
                              %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                              %mi λ
                          %mtd
                            %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                            %mo =
                            %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                            %mrow
                              %mo |
                              %msub
                                %mi ssYT
                                %mi λ
                              %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                              %mi N
                              %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                              %mo |
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                          %mtd
                            %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                            %mo =
                            %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                            %munder
                              %mo{:lspace => "thinmathspace", :rspace => "thinmathspace"} ∏
                              %mrow
                                %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                                %mi i
                                %mo ,
                                %mi j
                                %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                            %mfrac
                              %mrow
                                %mi N
                                %mo +
                                %mi content
                                %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                                %mi i
                                %mo ,
                                %mi j
                                %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                              %mrow
                                %mi ℓ
                                %msub
                                  %mi hook
                                  %mi λ
                                %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                                %mi i
                                %mo ,
                                %mi j
                                %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                    %mo ,
                    %mphantom
                      %mi AAAA
                    %mi N
                    %mo ∈
                    %msub
                      %mi ℕ
                      %mo +
                    %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                    %mo .
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    \\begin{aligned}
                    \\frac
                    {  \chi^{(\lambda)}(e) }
                    { n!  }
                    N^n
                    \\cdot
                    EigVals[e^{- ln(N)} \cdot d_C]_\lambda
                    \&amp;
                    \\;=\;
                    \\left\vert ssYT_\lambda(N) \right\vert
                    \\\
                    \&amp;
                    \\;=\;
                    \\underset{(i,j)}{\prod}
