            %p Here we used:
            %ol
              %li
                %p
                  the Frobenius formula for Schur functions (
                  %a{:href => "Schur+function#FrobeniusFormula"}> this Prop.
                  );
              %li
                %p some evident re-arrangements;
              %li
                %p
                  the character formula for the eigenvalues (
                  %a{:href => "#CharacterFormulaForEigenvalues"}> this Prop
                  ).
            %p
              This shows the first part of the statement. Finally, that the eigenvalues for
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
